| 13:26:17 | Sender 2 | SIGNAL  |

Newest signals should appear first.

### Architecture

Do NOT try to make the website communicate directly with ESP-NOW.

The intended architecture is:

```text
ESP32 Sender 1 ──┐
                  │
ESP32 Sender 2 ──┼── ESP-NOW ──> ESP32 Master
                  │                  │
                  │                  │
                  │                  ▼
                  │              Internet
                  │                  │
                  │                  ▼
                  └────────────> Website
```

The Master ESP32 will eventually be responsible for forwarding received signals to the website over the internet.

For now, implement the **website/backend side of this integration** using a clean API/WebSocket architecture so that the ESP32 Master can send events to it.

Create an endpoint/API such as:

```text
POST /api/signal
```

with JSON such as:

```json
{
  "senderID": 1,
  "message": "SIGNAL",
  "timestamp": "2026-08-13T13:25:04"
}
```

The backend should validate the incoming data and broadcast the signal to connected website clients in real time.

Prefer **WebSockets or Server-Sent Events** for real-time browser updates rather than requiring the browser to constantly refresh or poll.

